From 633f068d55230388173306a0ae37035fd7826e2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 04:47:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/49] S020 (restore): the second pass decodes trees without
 keeping content IDs

From the S020 incumbent (T2). The trees that restore's second pass
(special files, hard links, metadata) reads again are decoded by
data.LoadMetadataTree: every content ID is still parsed by the ordinary
ID parser, but the slices are not kept. Planning and verification keep
using LoadTree.

Repair on top of S020's file: the decoder skipped strconv.Unquote for
every name without a backslash, so a name with a raw quote or newline
was accepted where stock rejects it (the R7 finding, copied into the
new decoder). It now uses nodeNameIsPlain, as the direct decoder does.
tree_metadata_name_test.go fails on S020's file (a raw quote is
accepted) and passes here: 37,750 adversarial trees agree with stock's
decoder, names and error text.

New: internal/data/tree_metadata.go, tree_metadata_test.go,
tree_metadata_name_test.go; internal/restorer/completion_settlement_test.go
(S020's test of file-stage settlement, unchanged).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
